From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sysfb: clip damage rectangle to scanout bounds

The destination address is calculated from the intersection of the plane and
damage rectangles, but the blitter receives the original damage rectangle.
If userspace supplies damage extending one line beyond the plane, the format
conversion loop writes one stride beyond the mapped system framebuffer.

Pass the intersected rectangle to the blitter as well. This keeps both its
dimensions and destination offset within the scanout mapping.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/drm_sysfb_modeset.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/drm_sysfb_modeset.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/drm_sysfb_modeset.c
index 71cd7ea..4e746d9 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/drm_sysfb_modeset.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/drm_sysfb_modeset.c
@@ -361,6 +361,6 @@ void drm_sysfb_plane_helper_atomic_update(struct drm_plane *plane, struct drm_at
 
 		iosys_map_incr(&dst, drm_fb_clip_offset(dst_pitch, dst_format, &dst_clip));
-		blit_to_crtc(&dst, &dst_pitch, shadow_plane_state->data, fb, &damage,
+		blit_to_crtc(&dst, &dst_pitch, shadow_plane_state->data, fb, &dst_clip,
 			     &shadow_plane_state->fmtcnv_state);
 	}
 
